					"patching_rect" : [ 430.0, 522.0, 589.0, 221.0 ],
					"text" : "Description of the Radio Station:\n\nElectroverse FM is an electronic sound-based generative radio station designed to create a dynamic and immersive soundscape inspired by the constantly shifting textures and rhythms of electronic music. The station features a blend of glitchy, rhythmic beats, and rich, modulated textures, all shaped by inputs such as time, rhythm, and user-controlled parameters. The name reflects the futuristic and boundless nature of the sounds, transporting listeners to a universe of electronic exploration.\n\nProject Overview:\n\nFor this patch, I used several gen~ example patches built into Max, including wave-shaping, phase modulation (PM), frequency modulation (FM), and other creative generative processing techniques. Each gen~ patcher was chosen to enhance the versatility of the soundscape, ensuring an interactive and adaptive radio station experience that evolves over time based on temporal inputs. I mapped these inputs to various aspects of the audio synthesis to simulate an evolving soundscape that captures the passage of time and evokes a dynamic radio broadcast."
				}

			}
, 			{
